---
/** The homepage's intro, in English. The layout is HomePage. */
import HomePage from '../../components/pages/HomePage.astro';
import NfxLogo from '../../components/NfxLogo.astro';
import DaeroLogo from '../../components/DaeroLogo.astro';
import OpenGivingLogo from '../../components/OpenGivingLogo.astro';
import RoboCupLogo from '../../components/RoboCupLogo.astro';
import PinPagLogo from '../../components/PinPagLogo.astro';
import Flag from '../../components/Flag.astro';
---

<HomePage>
	<Fragment slot="intro">
		<p class="lede">
			The biggest thing I’ve built is <OpenGivingLogo href="/work/opengiving/" preview="opengiving" />, a
			marketplace where part of every sale goes to a fundraising campaign. I wrote all
			the code for it: web, iOS and Android apps, and the backend API they share.
		</p>
		<p>
			I grew up in <span class="nowrap">São Paulo <Flag country="br" label="Brazil" /></span>. Currently, I am studying at
			<span class="nowrap"><a href="https://www.brown.edu/" rel="noopener" data-preview="school-brown">Brown</a> <Flag country="us" label="United States" /></span> until May 2027, pursuing an MS in Entrepreneurship, and studying
			cybersecurity at <a href="https://www.harvard.edu/" rel="noopener" data-preview="school-harvard">Harvard</a> (cross-registered in person). Before Brown I
			was the first engineering hire at <DaeroLogo href="/work/zeropunch/" preview="zeropunch" />, a construction software startup
			in Boston backed by <NfxLogo preview="org-nfx" />. I spent ten months leading their iOS app dev,
			while also supporting the web, infra and backend work.
		</p>
		<p>
			I got my B.Sc. in Computer Engineering at <a href="https://www.insper.edu.br/" rel="noopener" data-preview="school-insper">Insper</a>. For my
			<a href="/work/pinpag-capstone/" data-preview="pinpag-capstone">capstone</a>, I worked on multi-cloud security
			monitoring for <PinPagLogo href="/work/pinpag-capstone/" preview="pinpag-capstone" />, a Brazilian payments company. Part of it was a Python tool that mapped how their AWS
			resources connected and flagged anything open to the internet that shouldn’t be.
			I was also on Insper Dynamics, a student team building rescue robots, for 2 years. We won
			a Best in Class award for sensing at <RoboCupLogo href="/work/robocup/" preview="robocup" /> in
			<span class="nowrap">2022 <Flag country="th" label="Bangkok, Thailand" /></span>,
			and one for exploration, the autonomous mapping test, in
			<span class="nowrap">2023 <Flag country="fr" label="Bordeaux, France" /></span>.
			In early 2023 I became president of the university’s robotics club.
		</p>
		<p class="contact">
			Email’s the easiest way to reach me:
			<a href="mailto:me@enriccogemha.dev">me@enriccogemha.dev</a>
		</p>
	</Fragment>
</HomePage>
